## 17. Data normalization and deduplication

Different providers may return the same business or opportunity.

Create a common normalized data model.

For business records, store:
- Business name.
- Category.
- Location.
- Address.
- Website.
- Public phone.
- Public email.
- Social links.
- Source.
- Source URL.
- Provider ID.
- Discovery timestamp.
- Last verified timestamp.

For hiring opportunities, store:
- Title.
- Original content.
- Company.
- Required service.
- Budget.
- Location.
- Employment/project type.
- Source URL.
- Publication date.
- Discovery date.
- AI classification.
- Confidence score.

Implement deduplication using normalized business names, domain names, addresses, provider IDs, and source URLs where available.

Do not merge records automatically when the match is uncertain. Flag them for review.

Clearly distinguish:
- Original source data.
- AI-generated analysis.
- User-added information.
- Verified information.

